# M15 on-target test fixture: wire=slip -- the "wire" sub-test asserts
# the whole non-Ethernet surface on unit 15: S2_DEVICEQUERY must report
# HardwareType=S2WireType_SLIP/AddrFieldSize=32 plus the per-wire
# mtu/bps defaults (1006/19200, neither overridden here on purpose),
# RawMTU=0; S2_GETSTATIONADDRESS must hand out the 4-byte
# 0A:53:32:<unit> factory address; S2_BROADCAST and a SANA2IOF_RAW write
# must both fail S2ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED; and a plain echo write/read
# round-trip must still work with 4-byte swapped addressing. Unit 15 is
# M15's own new unit (SANA2LOOP_NUM_UNITS 15 -> 16) -- the first unit
# growth since the pre-launch pass moved the memory floor to 2 MB, which
# is what made growth affordable again (see that constant's comment).
wire=slip
